[21.568, "o", "Comparing local manifests with the cluster (v1.29.4)\r\n\r\n\u001b[33m~\u001b[0m \u001b[1mDeployment/orders-api\u001b[0m [shop]  6 change(s)\r\n    spec.replicas: \u001b[31m2\u001b[0m \u2192 \u001b[32m4\u001b[0m\r\n    spec.selector.matchLabels.app: \u001b[31morders\u001b[0m \u2192 \u001b[32morders-api\u001b[0m\r\n    spec.template.spec.containers[api].image: \u001b[31mghcr.io/example/orders-api:2.2.0\u001b[0m \u2192 \u001b[32mghcr.io/example/orders-api:2.3.1\u001b[0m\r\n    spec.template.spec.containers[api].resources.requests.cpu: \u001b[31m500m\u001b[0m \u2192 \u001b[32m4\u001b[0m\r\n    spec.template.spec.containers[api].resources.requests.memory: \u001b[31m512Mi\u001b[0m \u2192 \u001b[32m8Gi\u001b[0m\r\n    spec.template.spec.containers[api].resources.limits.memory: \u001b[31m512Mi\u001b[0m \u2192 \u001b[32m8Gi\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[31m\u2716 error  \u001b[0m \u001b[2mDF001\u001b[0m  spec.selector is immutable (live: matchLabels: {app: orders}): apply will fail; delete and recreate (downtime) or deploy under a new name and migrate traffic\r\n  \u001b[33m\u26a0 warning\u001b[0m \u001b[2mDF006\u001b[0m  spec.replicas (4) is set but HorizontalPodAutoscaler \"orders-api\" manages this workload: every apply resets it to 4 (currently 2); remove spec.replicas from the manifest\r\n  \u001b[36m\u2139 info   \u001b[0m \u001b[2mDF007\u001b[0m  image change: api: ghcr.io/example/orders-api:2.2.0 -> ghcr.io/example/orders-api:2.3.1\r\n  \u001b[36m\u2139 info   \u001b[0m \u001b[2mDF007\u001b[0m  pod template changed: triggers a rolling restart of 4 pod(s)\r\n\u001b[32m+\u001b[0m \u001b[1mHorizontalPodAutoscaler/orders-api\u001b[0m [shop]  new (will be created)\r\n\u001b[33m~\u001b[0m \u001b[1mService/orders-api\u001b[0m [shop]  1 change(s)\r\n    spec.ports[0].port: \u001b[31m443\u001b[0m \u2192 \u001b[32m80\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[33m\u26a0 warning\u001b[0m \u001b[2mDF005\u001b[0m  Service port 443 is removed: existing clients using the old port will break\r\n\r\n1 new, 2 changed, 0 unchanged \u2014 1 breaking/error, 2 warning(s), 2 info\r\n"]
